&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
margin-left:0cm;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;
font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The
principle of the access point and lack of any urban design to enhance this rear
service area to provide a legible and permeable use with an active frontage is
unacceptable. The submitted information provides insufficient information with
regards to access, entrance ways, a shopfront, signage, or a designated pathway
for the new unit in the rear service area. As such, it fails to provide a safe,
permeable, or legible physical and visual connection that would knit well into
the surrounding streets and public realm and it cannot be determined to be
contribute positively to the Primary Shopping Area or the healthy streets
approach and is therefore contrary to Policy 40, 41, 45, 53 of Waltham Forests
LP1 (2024)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;and T2 of
the London Plan (2021).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB&quot;&gt;It is
unevidenced and unclear as to whether there would be adequate space and arrangements
for the storage and collection of refuse and recycling given the conflict of
uses for the entrance point to the proposed unit and therefore the application
cannot be determined to comply with Policies 57 and 93 of the adopted Waltham
Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
